Enhancement: Add `--atomic` option to the `restore` command

The `restore` command now supports an `--atomic` option. The selected snapshot
is first restored into a hidden temporary directory next to the target
directory, including files, directories, hard links, metadata and the
deletions requested by `--delete`. Only after the complete restore succeeds is
the temporary directory switched into place. If the restore is canceled or
fails at any point before that, the target directory remains in its previous
state. The option can be combined with the existing overwrite, filter, sparse
and dry-run options, which keep their usual behavior.
